/* d_a_obj_light_t60.h (WWHD, true 60 build; generated by tools/t60conv, 2026-11-17): d_a_obj_light.cpp on a general step
 * length (dt = 1/N). Decomp build only.
 *
 * Converted, the actor executes on every step with g_dt = 1/N; at dt = 1 (N = 1, the 30 Hz fallback, an unconverted
 * actor) every helper returns the original per-frame value (dt-1 check bit-exact). The helpers are the shared ones of
 * d/t60conv.h; d_a_obj_light.cpp keeps thin calls only.
 *
 * Sites (the tool's draft, finished by hand, 2026-11-17):
 *   exe_fire       the fire flicker (phase, rotation, scale, alpha, matrix) whole on the frame's first step (30 Hz visual-motion: the
 *                  phase stays on the 30 Hz grid; values derived from it before its add would end the frame mid-phase)
 *   exe_event      frame-level logic on the first step (first-step AI-timer / first-step frame-level)
 *   renew_angle    the beam's turn: t60c::share of 64 / 128 per frame (exact per frame)
 *   set_collision  the TG hit held over the frame (t60c::hit, mixed-pair hit-flag); lighting it (mLit, mLightTimer = 1) on the tick30
 *                  step: _execute calls set_collision after renew_angle, so no earlier step of the frame may see it
 *   control_light  the light timer, event bits and the event order on the tick30 step (_execute calls it last)
 *   _execute       mBgW->Move per step (the base does not move: review item)
 *
 * Not in kT60Converted: the profile is added after the paired runs. */
